{"title":"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25619b168b13802d30603e0b394037b2b0a2be5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1n = 0.d_1d_2d_3d_4\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />, an infinite decimal that has the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245551e06664fe19f066db1c096c6b8efbb1a5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i = d_{i+12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />. Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e61ce09efe3f712dc81b4013adc833fb23dbb813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9901$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> is prime, how many positive integers are in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />? (The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f1544d77330dc5a289ad6a42beeb236b8dd70a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> are digits.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/033fbaba6e1e52407308b324a74e86505aa5eac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = d_1 d_2 d_3 \\ldots d_{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"15\" />, the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> decimal digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/c/d4c13e6f961c9bff23cc9fe69c37050986eb4b38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"10\" height=\"21\" />. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56fc344d86abd1edf2f0f33a1f799c7aafc33892.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(10^{12} - 1)\\left(\\dfrac{1}{n}\\right) = k \\implies kn = 10^{12} - 1,\\]\" width=\"316\" height=\"43\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is the set that contains all divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a574cbd321b6074ce34a61ec6c566596f60fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{12} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114b6274040054a41dae6e5c0b7f4ee5d75ee0a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10^{12} - 1 = (10^6 + 1)(10^6 - 1) = (10^2 + 1)(10^4 - 10^2 + 1)(10^3 + 1)(10^3 - 1) = 101 \\cdot 9901 \\cdot 37 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 13 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 3^3 \\cdot 37,\\]\" width=\"745\" height=\"19\" /> the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/9/4692a14d7efebd3d8e0048703ca0f5916bd6ec3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{12} -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782140c9808d510dff756e0ece2a725f4946f5c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 2^6 = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" /> divisors and our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/1/6d13950de51924a917c79ea72feb1b357986ebb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256 - 1 = \\boxed{255}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-MP8148\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=14769\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_A